:"entity has at most one parent, and despawning a parent despawns its children, and theirs in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"turn. Build a hierarchy with "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/addChild(_:to:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", which refuses a link that would make"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"an entity its own ancestor, and walk it with "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/parent(of:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/children(of:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/ancestors(of:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/World\/descendants(of:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The following example attaches a turret and an engine to a ship, then despawns the ship,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which takes its parts with it:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["var world = World()","let ship = world.spawn(Name(value: \"Ship\"))","let turret = world.spawn(Name(value: \"Turret\"))","let engine = world.spawn(Name(value: \"Engine\"))","try world.addChild(turret, to: ship)","try world.addChild(engine, to: ship)","","let parts = world.children(of: ship).map { world[Name.self, of: $0].value }","print(parts)","\/\/ Prints \"[\"Turret\", \"Engine\"]\"","","world.despawn(ship)","print(world.contains(engine))","\/\/ Prints \"false\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"ChildOf","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Relation","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" like any other, so an entity with a parent holds a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"Targets<ChildOf>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" component naming it. Queries use that to find the entities at each level"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of a tree:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":".related(ChildOf.self, to: parent)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" keeps the children of ","type":"text"},{"code":"parent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".with(Targets<ChildOf>.self)"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps entities that have a parent."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".without(Targets<ChildOf>.self)"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps the roots."}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["var world = World()","let menu = world.spawn(Name(value: \"Menu\"))","let play = world.spawn(Name(value: \"Play\"))","let quit = world.spawn(Name(value: \"Quit\"))","try world.addChild(play, to: menu)","try world.addChild(quit, to: menu)","","print(world.query(Name.self).related(ChildOf.self, to: menu).count)","\/\/ Prints \"2\"","print(world.query(Name.self).without(Targets<ChildOf>.self).count)","\/\/ Prints \"1\""]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/worldmodule\/childof"]}],"metadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ChildOf","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"struct","modules":[{"name":"WorldModule"}],"title":"ChildOf","externalID":"s:11WorldModule7ChildOfV","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","remoteSource":{"fileName":"Hierarchy.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/ECS\/blob\/main\/Sources\/WorldModule\/Hierarchy.swift#L51"},"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind